PsychoticMuffin wrote:
> 1. What do ring of polymorph & polymorph control do and how do you use them?

A ring must be worn to have any effect.  Wearing a ring of polymorph
will cause you to occaisionally turn into other, random, things.  The
change isn't permanent, but it's possible for armor you're wearing to
be destroyed in a change.  Weak characters have a chance of dying of
system shock in the process (I think poly control and shock resistance
protect against that, though).

A ring of polymorph control means, when you change, you get to pick
what you turn into.  The game will ask you for the name of the monster
you want to become.  If you enter something not in the game, you'll
become something random.


> 2. How long can you polymorph for at maximum? Cause I used a scroll of
> polymorph and polymorphed into a balrog on level 1, but after like 10 or
> 20 turns I went back to my gnome form.

The stronger the monster is relative to your level, the shorter it'll
last.  You also turn back if you run out of hit points.  If you put on
an amulet of unchanging after the transformation you'll never turn
back, but you'll die if you run out of hit points.


> And then anything else I need to know about polymorphing, cause I really
> want to learn how it can be useful.

Polymorph is one of Nethack's signature features.  It is possible to
turn into most types of non-unique, non-human monsters in the game, and
there are some forms with unique abilities that can't be gained in any
other way.  Xorns, vampire lords, various types of dragons (especially
black), demons and purple worms are just some of the more interesting
choices.

